  "narrative": "Features Several layers of obfuscation Payload and its immediate loader are .NET assemblies Initial loader uses the CppHostCLR[2] technique to inject and execute the .NET loader assembly Payload encrypted and stored under Microsoft. It can collect system information, download and execute applications, upload files, log keystrokes, grab screenshots/camera captures, retrieve system passwords and run shell commands. README.md from Quasar GitHub repository Behaviour The .NET payload is a heavily obfuscated backdoor based on an open-source remote administration tool called QuasarRAT[3].",
